\stxKnowl{
\begin{enumerate}
\item
\stxKnowl{
Suppose a student of yours is asked to complete the following fraction modeling task:

Given the number line below, mark the value \(\dfrac{7}{6}\).

Construct the desired model. Then \textbf{explain} each step of its construction process. How is the denominator represented in the model? How is the numerator represented? How does each inform the construction process?

 \includegraphics{assets/F2-E/generated/0359/p1_prob_model.png} 

\stxOuttro{
 \includegraphics{assets/F2-E/generated/0359/p1_ans_model.png} 

The denominator of 6 tells us to split the whole (represented the distance of 18 spaces between 0 and 1) into 6 equal parts. The numerator of 7 tells us to select 7 of the 6 parts. We show this selection by placing our point 21 spaces to the right of 0. Thus, we have a model of the fraction 7/6.

}
}

\end{enumerate}
}

